From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:52:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Reset a corrupt database when it is opened

The owner's decision on corrupt databases: reset them at open, as Gecko
does (CreateStorageConnection deletes a database that is corrupt when it
opens it and opens an empty one). A page that creates its stores in
upgradeneeded keeps working; the lost data couldn't be read anyway.

- SqlEngine::new deletes a database whose open (the schema check, the
  table creation, the metadata read) fails with a corruption error
  (SQLITE_CORRUPT, SQLITE_NOTADB, RDB_E_SQLITE_CORRUPT) and opens it
  anew, with a warning. RDB fails to open a file that isn't an SQLite
  database with a generic error (14800000), so the RDB executor reports
  such a failure as SqlError::NotADatabase when the file has content
  that doesn't start with the SQLite header. The executors delete the
  files without opening the database (SqlExecutor::delete_files): SQLite
  removes the file and its -wal, -shm and -journal files, RDB calls
  OH_Rdb_DeleteStoreV2 once the failed store handle is closed.
- Corruption found while the database is in use still force-closes its
  connections (stack 185). The next open of a database that was marked
  unusable, once those connections are closed, deletes its files before
  it opens it.

The registry entry and directory stay, so the database is created anew in
the same directory and the page gets upgradeneeded from version 0.
Deleting a corrupt database of an earlier session still deletes it and
reports version 0.

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 168 passed, 1 skipped (new backend tests on each executor: corrupt_database_is_reset_when_opened, garbage in the database file, and injected_corruption_at_open_resets_the_database, a corruption that the Faulty executor reports for the first statement of the open, while another failure there resets nothing; new integration tests test_indexeddb_corrupt_database_is_reset_when_opened, garbage written between two sessions: databases() omits it, the next open upgrades from 0 in the same registry directory, and databases() lists it with version 1, also after a restart, and test_indexeddb_corrupt_database_of_an_earlier_session_is_deleted, which reports version 0); DAYU200 `./mach test-unit --ohos -p servo-storage`: RDB only 168 passed, 3 skipped, both backends 304 passed, 4 skipped (the RDB variants of both garbage-file tests failed with 14800000 from OH_Rdb_CreateOrOpen until the RDB executor reported it as NotADatabase); `./mach check --ohos` of servo-storage with SQLite, RDB and both: no warnings; WPT on the stack tip as in 182. Not covered by a test: the reset of a database that a failure marked unusable during a session, the manager path, as an open database can't be corrupted on disk reliably
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent implemented the reset in the engine, the executors and the manager, wrote the backend and integration tests and ran them on the board)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
